{"questions":[{"question_id":"luxzq9jw","content":"<p>The incorrect statement regarding ethyne is</p>","chapter":"hydrocarbons","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 9th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pthe-incorrect-statement-regarding-ethyne-isp-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-6luvvtmdc98verm6","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The incorrect statement regarding ethyne is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The carbon - carbon bonds in ethyne is weaker than that in ethene\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both carbons are sp hybridised\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds in ethyne is shorter than that in ethene\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Ethyne is linear"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>To evaluate which statement regarding ethyne is incorrect, it's necessary to review the characteristics of the chemical bonds in ethyne (acetylene, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) compared to ethene (ethylene, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option A:</strong> The statement that the carbon-carbon bonds in ethyne are weaker than that in ethene is <strong>incorrect</strong>. In ethyne, the carbon-carbon triple bond is composed of one sigma (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) bond and two pi (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) bonds. This configuration makes the triple bond in ethyne much stronger and shorter compared to the double bond in ethene, which consists of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Thus, the carbon-carbon bond in ethyne is actually stronger than that in ethene. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option B:</strong> The statement that both carbons are sp hybridised in ethyne is <strong>correct</strong>. In ethyne, each carbon atom is bonded to the other carbon atom and a single hydrogen atom, necessitating the sp hybridisation to form a linear molecule with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> angles between the bonds. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option C:</strong> The statement that the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds in ethyne are shorter than that in ethene is <strong>correct</strong>. The presence of a triple bond between the carbon atoms in ethyne results in a shorter bond length compared to the double-bonded carbons in ethene. This is because the additional pi bonds in a triple bond pull the carbon atoms closer together. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option D:</strong> The statement that ethyne is linear is <strong>correct</strong>. Due to the sp hybridisation of carbon atoms in ethyne, the molecule adopts a linear geometry with bond angles of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. </p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the incorrect statement regarding ethyne is <strong>Option A</strong>: The carbon-carbon bonds in ethyne are weaker than that in ethene.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>इथाइन से सम्बन्धित गलत कथन है:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"इथाइन में, एथीन की तुलना में, कार्बन-कार्बन आबन्ध दुर्बल है।\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"दोनों ही कार्बन <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.149ex\" height=\"1.452ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -448 950 642\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> संकरित हैं।\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"एथाइन में, एथीन की तुलना में, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> आबन्ध छोटा है।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"इथाइन रेखीय है।\n"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>यह मूल्यांकन करने के लिए कि एथाइन के संबंध में कौन सा कथन गलत है, एथीन (एथिलीन, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) की तुलना में एथाइन (एसिटिलीन, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) में रासायनिक बंधों की विशेषताओं की समीक्षा करना आवश्यक है।</p>\n\n<p><strong>विकल्प A:</strong> यह कथन कि एथाइन में कार्बन-कार्बन बंध एथीन की तुलना में कमजोर हैं, <strong>गलत</strong> है। एथाइन में, कार्बन-कार्बन त्रि-बंध एक सिग्मा (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) बंध और दो पाई (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) बंधों से बना होता है। यह विन्यास एथाइन में त्रि-बंध को एथीन में द्वि-बंध की तुलना में बहुत अधिक मजबूत और छोटा बनाता है, जो एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध और एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध से मिलकर बना होता है। इस प्रकार, एथाइन में कार्बन-कार्बन बंध वास्तव में एथीन की तुलना में मजबूत होता है।</p>\n\n<p><strong>विकल्प B:</strong> यह कथन कि एथाइन में दोनों कार्बन sp संकरित हैं, <strong>सही</strong> है। एथाइन में, प्रत्येक कार्बन परमाणु दूसरे कार्बन परमाणु और एक हाइड्रोजन परमाणु से बंधित होता है, जिससे बंधों के बीच <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> कोण के साथ एक रैखिक अणु बनाने के लिए sp संकरण आवश्यक हो जाता है।</p>\n\n<p><strong>विकल्प C:</strong> यह कथन कि एथाइन में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध एथीन की तुलना में छोटे हैं, <strong>सही</strong> है। एथाइन में कार्बन परमाणुओं के बीच त्रि-बंध की उपस्थिति के परिणामस्वरूप एथीन में द्वि-बंधित कार्बन की तुलना में छोटी बंध लंबाई होती है। ऐसा इसलिए है क्योंकि त्रि-बंध में अतिरिक्त पाई बंध कार्बन परमाणुओं को एक-दूसरे के करीब खींचते हैं।</p>\n\n<p><strong>विकल्प D:</strong> यह कथन कि एथाइन रैखिक है, <strong>सही</strong> है। एथाइन में कार्बन परमाणुओं के sp संकरण के कारण, अणु <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के बंध कोण के साथ एक रैखिक ज्यामिति अपनाता है।</p>\n\n<p>इसलिए, एथाइन के संबंध में गलत कथन <strong>विकल्प A</strong> है: एथाइन में कार्बन-कार्बन बंध एथीन की तुलना में कमजोर हैं।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"properties-and-preparation-of-alkynes","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The carbon - carbon bonds in ethyne is weaker than that in ethene\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both carbons are sp hybridised\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds in ethyne is shorter than that in ethene\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Ethyne is linear"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>To evaluate which statement regarding ethyne is incorrect, it's necessary to review the characteristics of the chemical bonds in ethyne (acetylene, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) compared to ethene (ethylene, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.306ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2345.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1158.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option A:</strong> The statement that the carbon-carbon bonds in ethyne are weaker than that in ethene is <strong>incorrect</strong>. In ethyne, the carbon-carbon triple bond is composed of one sigma (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) bond and two pi (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) bonds. This configuration makes the triple bond in ethyne much stronger and shorter compared to the double bond in ethene, which consists of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Thus, the carbon-carbon bond in ethyne is actually stronger than that in ethene. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option B:</strong> The statement that both carbons are sp hybridised in ethyne is <strong>correct</strong>. In ethyne, each carbon atom is bonded to the other carbon atom and a single hydrogen atom, necessitating the sp hybridisation to form a linear molecule with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> angles between the bonds. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option C:</strong> The statement that the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.033ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2666.4 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1944.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds in ethyne are shorter than that in ethene is <strong>correct</strong>. The presence of a triple bond between the carbon atoms in ethyne results in a shorter bond length compared to the double-bonded carbons in ethene. This is because the additional pi bonds in a triple bond pull the carbon atoms closer together. </p>\n\n<p><strong>Option D:</strong> The statement that ethyne is linear is <strong>correct</strong>. Due to the sp hybridisation of carbon atoms in ethyne, the molecule adopts a linear geometry with bond angles of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. </p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the incorrect statement regarding ethyne is <strong>Option A</strong>: The carbon-carbon bonds in ethyne are weaker than that in ethene.</p>"}]}